From bb3052f35847f55b08b09d227f602d8c4d797345 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 01:30:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Rotation matrices: exported material axes, copies of the
 local storage

- MaterialAxisStorage is exported: copying a RotationMatrix2D or a
  RotationMatrix3D outside of MGIS failed to link (destructor not
  exported).
- the copy of a material axis stored locally refers to its own values;
  it referred to the values of the original, which dangled once the
  original was destroyed. A material axis stored in an external array
  still refers to this array. Copy and move constructors of the rotation
  matrices.
- the constructor of MaterialAxisStorage from a temporary vector, which
  was declared, is defined.
---
